ce:section.ce:para:
Toxicity data obtained from the literature and the present study are summarized in Table S5. The PNEC value was calculated by the AF method and the SSD methods (Table 1
                         and Fig. 3
                        ). The lowest NOEC values for BPA, BPS, and BPSIP were 16 μg/L (Sohoni et al., 2001), 1 μg/L (Naderi et al., 2014), and 100 μg/L (this study), respectively. Because chronic toxicity data are available from test organisms of three trophic levels, i.e., algae, daphnids, and fishes for all tested bisphenols, an AF of 10 was used. PNECAF values were 1.6 μg/L for BPA, 0.1 μg/L for BPS, and 10 μg/L for BPSIP (Table 1).
